{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793553349,"nonce":"oLsiVTSf2zVjj+ncfh9TFbFXlzc=","message":"Measurement pitfall found while testing promotion policy: any ZYNTAX_* variable outside a short list switches off portable (ahead-of-time) library code. zyntax_embed::snapshot::portable_code_allowed accepts only ZYNTAX_TRACE_*, ZYNTAX_DUMP_*, ZYNTAX_COMPILE_WORKERS, ZYNTAX_DISABLE_WARM_UP, ZYNTAX_OPTIMIZE_QUIET_MS and ZYNTAX_PORTABLE_COMPILE_AT_LOAD. The same binary with `ZYNTAX_DUMMY_UNUSED=1` set runs the zypy suite (12 kernels, 9 runs, 4 pinned cores) 4.2% slower on the score, 2.5% on wall, 4.1% on CPU: chaos +6%, deltablue +16%, richards +13%, spectral +14%. Any A/B where one arm sets a knob and the other does not measures that, not the knob: give both arms a knob from the list, or set the knob in both. Three earlier comparisons in this thread were affected (the nice test, the cold-path decomposition, the callees-first/threshold knobs); the 20 ms vs spare-core comparison used the allowed variable and stands.","files":null}]}